    [Refactor][Patch] Remove obsolete DeepSeek V4 vision converter (#18884)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    vLLM v0.31 natively routes DeepSeek-V4 vision checkpoints to
    `DeepseekV4ForConditionalGeneration` and sets the multimodal prefix
    metadata required by the Ascend path. The Ascend compatibility converter
    therefore duplicates upstream behavior and is no longer needed.
    
    This PR removes:
    
    - `vllm_ascend/patch/platform/patch_deepseek_v4_vision.py`;
    - its platform patch import;
    - its registration call from `NPUPlatform.pre_register_and_update()`;
    and
    - its patch documentation entry.
    
    The Ascend model registry mapping for
    `DeepseekV4ForConditionalGeneration` remains unchanged.
    
    Upstream references:
    
    - https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/54566
    -
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/main/vllm/transformers_utils/model_arch_config_convertor.py
    -
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/main/vllm/transformers_utils/configs/deepseek_v4.py
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    No. This removes a redundant compatibility patch now that the supported
    vLLM version provides the same DeepSeek-V4 vision config conversion
    natively.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - `git diff --check`
    - `python -m compileall -q vllm_ascend/platform.py
    vllm_ascend/patch/platform/__init__.py vllm_ascend/patch/__init__.py`
    - `ruff check vllm_ascend/platform.py
    vllm_ascend/patch/platform/__init__.py vllm_ascend/patch/__init__.py`
    - Verified no remaining references to `patch_deepseek_v4_vision` or
    `register_deepseek_v4_vision_config_convertor`.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/c4df37dfcc7f72ca41cd43801a468526ecf99a2b
    
    Signed-off-by: QwertyJack <7554089+QwertyJack@users.noreply.github.com>
    Co-authored-by: QwertyJack <7554089+QwertyJack@users.noreply.github.com>

